        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Hua Hin, Thailand, Cambodia\n- Hotels: The Railway Hotel, Hua Hin; Hotel Phnom Penh\n- Films: The Killing Fields\n- People: Dith Pran, Sydney Schanberg\n- Topics: Khmer Rouge regime, journalism\n\nFacts:\n- The Railway Hotel is a historic hotel in Hua Hin, Thailand.\n- In 1984, the film The Killing Fields used The Railway Hotel as the Hotel Phnom Penh.\n- The Killing Fields is a 1984 British biographical drama film about the Khmer Rouge regime in Cambodia.\n- The Killing Fields is based on the experiences of the journalists Dith Pran of Cambodia and Sydney Schanberg of the United States.",
